<title>GREECE: PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) TO RAISE GASOLINE PRICES JAN 16.</title>
<headline>PUBLIC PETROLEUM (DEP) TO RAISE GASOLINE PRICES JAN 16.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Public Petroleum Corporation (DEP) will raise gasoline prices by 0.2 drachmas per litre on Thursday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Transport diesel prices will drop by 1.0 drachmas a litre and heating fuel prices will stay unchanged.</p>
<p>The price adjustments reflect lower international gasoline and diesel prices, down by $0.7 and $5.8 per metric tonne respectively, and a higher dollar/drachma exchange rate, DEP said. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
